audited	w_ee7cdd8c7d281656	A simple model of co-emergence of grid and place fields	INCLUDE	explicit-claims-results	770	147	0	0	Title: A simple model of co-emergence of grid and place fields. Claim: A single predictive RNN develops complementary grid- and place-like spatial codes without spatial supervision. Supporting result: Neither cell type nor allocentric coordinates are supplied; formal field metrics characterize the learned codes, while architecture removals and new-environment experiments show the recurrent state uses the organization for next-sensory prediction. Claim: Noise, masking, memory decay, environment, and training time reorganize the balance of spatial codes. Supporting result: One thousand parameter configurations, ten-seed replication, architectural controls, and developmental trajectories connect place/grid population regimes to the sensory-prediction computation.
