audited	w_f05eeedb3d84fbb7	The Geometry of Multi-Task Grokking: Transverse Instability, Superposition, and Weight Decay Phase Structure	INCLUDE	explicit-claims-results	1642	324	0	0	Title: The Geometry of Multi-Task Grokking: Transverse Instability, Superposition, and Weight Decay Phase Structure. Claim: (2) Universal integrability: optimization trajectories remain confined to an empirically invariant low-dimensional execution manifold; commutator defects orthogonal to this manifold reliably precede generalization. Supporting result: Synthesis.Together, these results show that generalization-relevant information is simultaneously low-dimensional (k∗ principal trajectory directions suffice for reconstruction) and globally distributed (full-rank weights, with every module necessary). Claim: A transverse-instability transition separates the memorizing and generalizing regimes. Supporting result: The rapid internal transition is replicated across modular operations and seeds; deleting orthogonal gradient components prevents the matched generalization transition while norm-matched controls do not. Claim: The Geometry of Multi-Task Grokking: Transverse Instability, Superposition, and Weight Decay Phase Structure. Supporting result: Unlike prior work that focuses on either representational superposition [Elhage et al., 2022] or learning dynamics in isolation [Davies et al., 2023, Kumar et al., 2024], our study combines trajectory geometry, curvature analysis, and causal perturbations to provide a unified dynamical account of multi-task grokking. Claim: Weight decay controls qualitative internal regimes in multi-task grokking. Supporting result: Checkpointed attention spectra and trajectory geometry vary across weight-decay, task, and seed controls in step with the memorization/generalization regimes.
audited	w_125db4c2cf79214e	The Geometry of Thought: How Scale Restructures Reasoning In Large Language Models	EXCLUDE	explicit-claims-results	1842	358	0	0	Title: The Geometry of Thought: How Scale Restructures Reasoning In Large Language Models. Claim: Analyzing 25,000+ chain-of-thought trajectories across four domains (Law, Science, Code, Math) and two scales (8B, 70B parameters), we discover that neural scaling laws trigger… Supporting result: Unless stated otherwise, all reported “decoding accuracy” in this paper refers to the adapter/probe regime; frozen-unembedding decoding is treated as a diagnostic and is not used as the headline accuracy metric in our experimental setting. 1.4 Preview of findings: a phase diagram of thought Our experiments reveal that reasoning geometry is not uniform across domains, and that scale induces domain-specific phase transitions rather than universal improvement. Claim: The Geometry of Thought: How Scale Restructures Reasoning In Large Language Models. Supporting result: These findings establish that the cost of thought is determined not by task difficulty but by manifold geometry—offering a blueprint for inference acceleration where topology permits. 1 Introduction The scaling hypothesis has become the central organizing principle of modern deep learning: larger models, trained on more data, yield predictably better performance across an expanding frontier of tasks. Claim: The Geometry of Thought: How Scale Restructures Reasoning In Large Language Models. Supporting result: Unless stated otherwise, all reported “decoding accuracy” in this paper refers to the adapter/probe regime; frozen-unembedding decoding is treated as a diagnostic and is not used as the headline accuracy metric in our experimental setting. 1.4 Preview of findings: a phase diagram of thought Our experiments reveal that reasoning geometry is not uniform across domains, and that scale induces domain-specific phase transitions rather than universal improvement.
